{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>You shall not consent to him.</b> Do not desire him; do not love him — for it is said (Leviticus 19) ״וְאָהַבְתָּ לְרֵעֲךָ כָּמוֹךָ״ — this one you shall not love." "<b>And you shall not listen to him.</b> When he pleads for his life to be spared — for it is said (Exodus 23) ״עָזֹב תַּעֲזֹב עִמּוֹ״ — this one you shall not help." "<b>And your eye shall not pity him.</b> For it is said (Leviticus 19) ״לֹא תַּעֲמֹד עַל דַּם רֵעֶךָ״ — this one you shall not pity." "<b>And you shall not spare.</b> Do not plead his merit." "<b>And you shall not shield him.</b> If you know of his liability you may not remain silent (Sifrei)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:46:56.197505873Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}